      "rationale": "Bare text length of the review. It is a property of the review text, not a cause of the flight being non-recommended; at most a proxy/collider driven by the reviewer's experience. Generic, mechanical feature with no causal standing."
    },
    {
      "name": "Rating_Variance",
      "causal_role": "collider",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Variance across the sub-ratings is a downstream summary of the same ratings that drive recommendation. It sits on/after the causal path (function of outcomes-correlated ratings), not a common cause of any treatment and the outcome."
    },
    {
      "name": "Complaint_Count",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Number of complaints extracted from the review reflects the negative experience that then leads to a non-recommendation. It lies on the causal path between the underlying service failures and the outcome, so it is a mediator, not a confounder."
    },
    {
      "name": "Low_Rating_Count",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Count of low sub-ratings is essentially the mechanism producing non-recommendation; a near-deterministic descendant of the ratings that drive the outcome, not a common cause."
    },
    {
      "name": "Has_Major_Complaint",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Presence of a major complaint is part of the causal path to non-recommendation, expressing the same dissatisfaction rather than an upstream common cause of a distinct treatment."
    },
    {
      "name": "Overall_Low",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Binarised low Overall Rating is a near-proxy of the recommendation decision itself; overall rating and recommendation are co-determined by the experience. It is a descendant/mediator, not a confounder."
    },
    {
      "name": "Service_Comfort_Gap",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Gap between service and comfort sub-ratings is a derived experience measure on the path to (non-)recommendation, not a common cause of a treatment and the outcome."
    }
  ],
  "treatment_present": false,
  "treatment_columns": [],
  "confounders": [],
  "confounder_quality": 0.0,
  "rationale": "No column is a candidate CAUSE (treatment) whose effect on non-recommendation is being attributed while being distinct from the outcome mechanism. Every substantive added column (Complaint_Count, Low_Rating_Count, Has_Major_Complaint, Overall_Low, Service_Comfort_Gap, Rating_Variance) is a downstream descendant/mediator/collider of the same dissatisfaction that determines recommendation, and Review_Length is a generic text feature. Crucially, the system supplied NO confounder -- no variable that plausibly causes both a treatment and the outcome (e.g., route difficulty, aircraft type, prior expectation, traveller sub-segment) is surfaced. Because there is neither a clean treatment nor any adjusted-for confounder, the causal-attribution claim is not realised."
}
